    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output today, anchored by **Trea Turner** (81.27) and **Yordan Alvarez** (77.03), both of whom boast elite efficiency ratings. **Trea Turner** is the clear priority; facing a soft matchup against Palmquist (6.00 xERA) combined with the opportunity to exploit a slow pitcher delivery makes him an elite target for our primary category, stolen bases. Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** and **Christian Yelich** (75.84) represent our strongest platoon-advantage plays, with **Christian Yelich** benefiting significantly from a favorable matchup against Lowder to elevate his stock. While **Caleb Durbin** sits at a robust 67.14, his efficiency is bolstered by a park factor surge, making him an essential piece of our middle-infield stack against Freeland.\n\nThe decision to bench **Luke Raley** (41.50) was the tightest call on the board. Although he holds a respectable platoon edge against Ashcraft, his low batting order placement and the defensive prowess of the opposing catcher (1.86s pop time) cannibalized his stolen base potential, effectively forcing him below our required efficiency floor. Conversely, **Nelson Velazquez** (51.27) secured a start over other reserves largely due to his elite xwOBA metrics, which outweigh the peripheral risks of his park factor. We are tracking **Pete Crow-Armstrong** closely; despite his favorable order spot, his efficiency is currently depressed (47.87) due to a brutal matchup against the tough Manaea and a severe platoon disadvantage. We advise monitoring wind conditions at the stadium, as any shift could further impact the projected output for **Carson Benge** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, though our primary roster remains set to maximize SB volume and efficient plate appearances.",
